# Session compositor profile: labwc. UNSUPPORTED EXAMPLE.
#
# Hermes ships and tests weston only. This file exists to show what a profile
# for another compositor looks like; rename it to labwc.conf (here, or in
# ~/.config/hermes/session-compositors/ to override without root) and set
# `hermes_kms_session_compositor = labwc` to try it. Nothing about it is
# verified, and problems with it are yours to debug.
#
# The reason it is interesting: wlroots takes the display device and the
# rendering device separately, and a render node carries no seat assignment.
# That is the one thing weston cannot express, and it is what would let a
# session render on the real GPU instead of falling back to llvmpipe.
#
# See weston.conf for the placeholder list.
requires = labwc
socket   = discovered
env      = WLR_DRM_DEVICES={card_path}, WLR_RENDER_DRM_DEVICE={render_node}, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR={runtime_dir}
command  = labwc
